Alicia &nbsp;Further to Matt’s email I believe the statement is ready for your review, together with the exhibit. Please see a clean version of the statement attached. &nbsp;Following a proofread I have made a couple of non-substantive amends. I have also updated the address to PG’s current address (Chancery House instead of Mark Lane). Please see the third attachment containing these proofreading amends if you would like to consider. &nbsp;&nbsp;Please do let me know if you have any comments or questions. &nbsp;Best Jess&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 19:22To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Yes, from our side.&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 19:05To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;Thanks all. I’ve reflected that amendment, and will share this updated wording with Theo who raised the question. &nbsp;Please see attached a proposed final draft of the statement in clean. Are we now at the point where Alicia can conduct a final review before signing off? I attach the exhibit as well for reference. &nbsp;BestJess&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Please note that our general terms and conditions apply to all our services. These general terms and conditions include a clause stipulating that our liability is excluded for damage caused by an event not covered by any insurance. The full general terms and conditions can be accessed via this link.​​Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of PGMBM Nederland B.V., a limited liability company registered at Chamber of Commerce (no. 83137718) with its registered office at Herengracht 433, 1017 BR Amsterdam. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.​​Deze e-mail en eventuele bijlagen zijn vertrouwelijk. Als u dit bericht ten onrechte ontvangt, neem dan onmiddellijk contact op met de afzender, vernietig de e-mail en eventuele bijlagen en gebruik, kopieer, bewaar of deel deze e-mail en eventuele bijlagen op geen enkele wijze. Pogust Goodhead aanvaardt geen betekening of kennisgeving van documenten langs elektronische weg zonder uitdrukkelijke voorafgaande toestemming.&nbsp;Op alle door Pogust Goodhead aanvaarde opdrachten zijn onze algemene voorwaarden van toepassing. De algemene voorwaarden bevatten onder meer een clausule waarin staat dat onze aansprakelijkheid is uitgesloten voor schade die niet door een verzekering wordt gedekt. De volledige tekst van onze algemene voorwaarden zijn toegankelijk via deze link.​Pogust Goodhead is de handelsnaam van PGMBM Nederland B.V., een naamloze vennootschap ingeschreven bij de Kamer van Koophandel (nr. 83137718), statutair gevestigd aan de Herengracht 433, 1017 BR Amsterdam. Voor meer informatie over welke persoonsgegeven wij verzamelen en waarom, zie onze Privacy Policy.From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 18:45To: 'Matthew Getz' &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;Thanks Matt, I agree. Can we pls go with this and then I understand this statement can be in final draft form. &nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 18:43To: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;I would make a single change beneath, and then I think this sets it out as accurately and clearly as it can without giving away too much information. I would stick with this.&nbsp;The Firm has sufficient funding to pay all expected outgoings until the conclusion of the PDD Trial hearing in December. Most recent funding has been provided by Gramercy, through two facilities made available on 14 August 2025 (the “August Trance”) and 19 September 2025 (the “September Tranche”). The August Tranche amounted to $65 million; the September Tranche was $30 million. While the August Tranche can be used for Firm overhead but not on specific NOx Group Litigations fees, the September Tranche can, contractually, only be used for the NOx Group Litigations. The funds held are made available by Gramercy &nbsp;and the Firm draws down on cash to service its working capital requirements monthly against these facilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 18:27To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;Anna, all,&nbsp;I sent the attached earlier, but I&nbsp;am unsure if it was reviewed. Was the decision to keep the current wording unchanged?&nbsp;Pallas, let me know if you'd like me to give drafting a try. I'm on another call at the moment, but I can work on it shortly.&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 14:06To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: Re: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;All&nbsp;Flicking this across for others to consider, while I field other points: @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;@Tom Crow@Helena Yearwood&nbsp;im sure you have already asnwered this but is this right: the $30m is held by Gramercy, but Gramercy is contractually obliged to release sums for Pan NOx on PG’s request? At the moment, I still find this paragraph a little unclear.&nbsp;&nbsp;This is the para:The Firm has sufficient cash to pay all expected outgoings until the conclusion of the PDD Trial hearing in December. Most recent funding has been provided by Gramercy, through two facilities made available on 14 August 2025 (the “August Trance”) and 19 September 2025 (the “September Tranche”). The August Tranche amounted to $65 million; the September Tranche was $30 million. While the August Tranche can be used for Firm overhead but not on specific NOx Group Litigations fees, the September Tranche can, contractually, only be used for the NOx Group Litigations. The funds held are made available by Gramercy &nbsp;and the Firm draws down on cash to service its working capital requirements monthly against these facilities.&nbsp;Anna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, September 30, 2025 5:56 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;In 37.1, we now have duplication in the last two sentences. If we have “The funds held are made available by Gramercy for PG to draw down in line with its cash needs.” Then we don’t need “The Firm draws down on cash to service its working capital requirements monthly against these facilities.” The first sentence is probably better37.4: Matthew Newbould is the leads37.5: Gladson, not Gladston37.7: either “some 12 solicitors working under the Case Leads on the…” or “an additional 12 solicitors on the…”&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 17:44To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: Re: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;All&nbsp;Latest version attached.&nbsp;&nbsp;Re the claimant sols committee - pls could pallas send me a proposed response this evening. I need to be in hospital but back at my desk by 8.30 to finalise and send.&nbsp;Anna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, September 30, 2025 5:28 PMTo: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;On para 22 (and sorry for my confusing draft agreements with executed agreements), do we know that the solicitors are in the process of entering into the agency agreements? If not, I think we should delete para 22 altogether. It isn’t that important&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 16:56To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;Thanks all. &nbsp;Two further points from Leigh Day:&nbsp;“Re para 22 - I don’t think this is correct - while I understand an AA has been executed in Merc I don’t think it has in the other Lead Cases.”&nbsp;Subject to any other views, we could amend the wording as follows: I note for completeness that the Lead Solicitors and other solicitors representing the Claimants in each Lead Case have separately entered into are separately entering into individual confidential agency agreements for each Lead Case governing the relationship between them.&nbsp;“Will you also refer to today’s letter from Cleary’s at para 41?”&nbsp;Please see the letter attached. I think it should be possible to add it without disrupting the pagination of the exhibit given it falls at the end of the bundle. @Xenia Kalognomas – please would you be able to add it to the exhibit? I’ll add the reference in the body of the statement.&nbsp;Many thanksJess &nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not us