Hi Anna, &nbsp;Hope you’re well and apologies for the late reply. &nbsp;We agreed the final versions of the priorities deeds with the insurers yesterday (including Toremis). We are now finalising the template claimant committee letter and aim to share it with you later today.&nbsp;Many thanks.&nbsp;Dilan&nbsp;From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 04 December 2025 13:58To: Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Claimant Committee Correspondence - Urgent feedback required &nbsp;Dilan&nbsp;Grateful for an update please.&nbsp;Thanks​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Saturday, November 29, 2025 5:00 PMTo: Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Claimant Committee Correspondence - Urgent feedback required &nbsp;Hi all&nbsp;One for Monday: but may I check where we got to with this workstream? Noting it is marked urgent and some time has now passed.&nbsp;Thanks​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Thursday, October 30, 2025 3:32 PMTo: Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Claimant Committee Correspondence - Urgent feedback required &nbsp;Hi Dilan,&nbsp;Sorry for taking ages to come back on this.&nbsp;My view is that we should err on the side of caution and seek Claimant Committee approval to the amendments to the ATE Priorities deed. That takes into account Clause 2 of the Mercedes LGA, which you highlighted as follows:&nbsp;“Clause 2. The parties to this Agreement appoint the Committee to be their agents in respect of the conduct of the litigation and empowers the Committee to enter into any such agreements as are necessary for the funding of the litigation and the procuring of insurance as against adverse costs risk.”&nbsp;I have attached a letter from the Hyundai litigation from August 2024, which shows that we informed the Claimant Committee of our proposals to increase the level of indemnity on ATE. I understand that similar letters were sent on each NOx case. We have therefore set the groundwork for this.&nbsp;I suggest we write to the Claimant Committees, referring back to these letters, confirming that we are now finalising the priorities deeds and seeking approval by way of FOA, and confirming the actual figures (additional indemnity and premium) if possible for completeness. We can also deal potentially deal with the demands and needs point raised in the same letter.&nbsp;Copying in @Sarah Bingham and @Anna Varga in case I have missed anything or there are different views.&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Matthew&nbsp;NewbouldPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;631From: Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 October 2025 14:23To: Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Claimant Committee Correspondence - Urgent feedback required &nbsp;Hi Matthew,&nbsp;Would you be able to come back to us on the matter below? Also, we have an additional question: can PG increase the ATE cover as it sees fit or do we need claimant committee’s consent for this?&nbsp;Many thanks.&nbsp;Dilan&nbsp;​​​​Dilan&nbsp;AlmaAssociate&nbsp;(General&nbsp;Counsel)From: Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 08 October 2025 18:38To: Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Claimant Committee Correspondence - Urgent feedback required &nbsp;Hi Matthew,&nbsp;I hope all is well.&nbsp;&nbsp;There is another matter we need your help with. You would recall from the correspondence below that when we were signing the priorities deeds last year, we reached out to the claimant committees to obtain their approval to sign the deeds on their behalf.&nbsp;&nbsp;Attached you'll find some examples of those authorisations. Following the top-up policies we are not executing an amendment to those previously signed PDs (nothing substantial just adding other excess layer insurers to the waterfall and some new amendments around the amount to be held on trust by PG for the ATE insurers). I have attached an example of the amended PDs (it is for FCA).&nbsp;The question is: as the claimants also need to sign this amended PDs, do you think we can rely on the previous authorisations given to us to sign on their behalf or shall we obtain a new one specifically for the amendments?&nbsp;Many thanks.&nbsp;Dilan&nbsp;​​​​Dilan&nbsp;AlmaAssociate&nbsp;(General&nbsp;Counsel)From:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;09 July 2024 12:37To:&nbsp;Samantha Imber &lt;simber@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;FW: Claimant Committee Correspondence - Urgent feedback required&nbsp;Merc FOAs&nbsp;Helena&nbsp;Yearwood​​​​Risk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom:&nbsp;Adam Melone &lt;amelone@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, June 12, 2024 4:35 PMTo:&nbsp;Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tony Winterburn &lt;twinterburn@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Peter Gallagher &lt;pgallagher@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Janice Tang &lt;jtang@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alex Tyerman &lt;atyerman@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jeremy Michael Evans &lt;jevans@pogustgoodhead.com&gt