s holding response dated 20 October to the Defendants in response to their letters of 17 OctoberLetter from Gramercy (BSF) dated 20 October in response to the Defendants letters of 17 OctoberLetter from Hogan Lovells dated 20 October in response to PG’s letter of 10 October &nbsp;Kind RegardsJess &nbsp;Jessica Fechner (she/her)Associate (England &amp; Wales qualified) Amsterdam &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 21 October 2025 13:57To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Theo, Simon&nbsp;Thank you both for your input in relation to 10 October letter. Simon - I understand you are in a heavy hearing at the moment - best of luck.&nbsp;&nbsp;Theo - we received several letters from Ds about the ATE and funding info disclosure (all within 1.5hrs on Friday evening). Besides a holding response, we are yet to respond substantively. There is a draft response in the works, which we will share today/tomorrow. In the meantime, I wanted to bring this to your attention - not least because any application for disclosure etc will be made 24th&nbsp;October. I've attached the relevant letters and the team will share the draft response once ready. Grateful for you input at such time. In addition, as will have been obvious to you both, we are in the process of sorting additional ATE and the team can update with details/timings.&nbsp;@Jessica Fechner&nbsp;please could you share (as sent) 10 October letter, holding response and check I have not omitted any correspondence on this topic.&nbsp;BestAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent: