 not consistent with the draft order, which simply has PG ceasing to be a Lead Solicitor.&nbsp; While you could include language in the statement referring to the possibility an application in the future seeking to be re-appointed, I suggest it would be simplest
 for the statement simply to remove references to ‘temporarily’.
&nbsp;
Martyn’s statement of yesterday makes clear in paragraph 20 that one of the reasons for stepping down and putting in place a firewall is to alleviate any concern of control by Gramercy.&nbsp; I appreciate,
 of course, that any suggestion of such control is firmly denied.&nbsp; However that concern is not referred to directly in Alicia’s draft statement as a reason for stepping down.&nbsp; The Defendants may argue that PG / Alicia are not being as frank as they should be
 about the reason for stepping down.
&nbsp;
It would be better if further detail could be given as to what is proposed to happen with the case leads, but I appreciate that may be difficult.
&nbsp;
