k on the Non-Common Work streams as required and directed solely by PG (which includes matters related to the non-Lead Cases, which are not subject to the Agency Agreement). If you have any regulatory concerns that you wish to inform the clients of, please let us know specifically what they are.We, LD and counsel – which has reviewed and signed off on the approach – are comfortable that this is an eminently workable solution which adheres to the existing legal framework and offers the best path forward in the best interests of our clients. We are happy for your to speak to counsel (mindful of the fact that they are also preparing for the PTR and trial). We welcome your input, some of which is being incorporated into the next round of the agency agreement and are obviously happy to deal with any further questions. However, we must make clear that your consent is not needed for us to enter into the agency agreement, as it does not represent a material change to our working relationship or your rights and responsibilities.Finally, we would never expect you to do anything in breach of your regulatory or professional obligations. The firm will always supervise its lawyers to safeguard from any potential breaches, and we trust you will do so at all times too, both on your own behalf and on behalf of those you supervise.Separately, a reminder that the updates to the PG claimants’ committees need to go out by close of play today. We would like you to send them. If you will not, then our duty to the clients will require me and Alicia to write to the committees ourselves&nbsp;Best, Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;GetzPartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInPallas Partners LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England with registered number OC437491, and is authorised and regulated by the 