 expenditure to July 2026 (when we expect to receive a decision on PDD). It would be helpful to confirm your /Simon’s views on us making these statements in the letter: &nbsp;Para 9a confirms that costs for the ADR/Settlement phase has not been included in the expenditure calculations as they have not yet been approved Para 9b confirms that costs for the Expert Reports phase have not been included in the expenditure calculations as they have not yet been approvedPara 13 confirms we are reducing the percentages applied to claimed incurred costs and costs of cost budgeting, the rationale being provided in para 16 (i.e. they are disproportionate and distort the sufficiency analysis)&nbsp;As discussed, these assumptions around calculating expenditure to the decision on PDD, which we believe are reasonable, help to demonstrate that we currently have sufficient cover. Once these points are factored into the calculations it is likely that the shortfall in ATE cover to July 26 will increase. &nbsp;Internally, we are working toward increasing our level of cover, however we know that there are issues around capacity in the market and there may be challenges in securing topups to our cover. We therefore do not feel that it is appropriate to disclose that we are looking to increase capacity in this letter. &nbsp;Please let us know your thoughts &nbsp;Regards Tom&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England a