Hi Anna&nbsp;Carol’s email on this chain was detailed and worth referring back to, but summarising below&nbsp;Technically yes, Gramercy are contractually committed to make advances up to the full facility amount. However, this obligation is subject to the satisfaction of conditions precedent which must be confirmed at the time of each advance request. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Firm has sufficient cash to pay all expected outgoings until the conclusion of the PDD Trial hearing in December. Most recent funding has been provided by Gramercy, through two facilities made available on 14 August 2025 (the “August Trance”) and 19 September 2025 (the “September Tranche”). The August Tranche amounted to $65 million; the September Tranche was $30 million. While the August Tranche can be used for Firm overhead but not on specific NOx Group Litigations fees, the September Tranche can, contractually, only be used for the NOx Group Litigations. The funds held are made available by Gramercy&nbsp;and the Firm draws down on cash to service its working capital requirements.&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 18:06To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: Re: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;All&nbsp;Flicking this across for others to consider, while I field other points: @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza&nbsp;@Tom Crow@Helena Yearwood&nbsp;im sure you have already asnwered this but is this right: the $30m is held by Gramercy, but Gramercy is contractually obliged to release sums for Pan NOx on PG’s request? At the moment, I still find this paragraph a little unclear.&nbsp;&nbsp;This is the para:The Firm has sufficient cash to pay all expected outgoings until the conclusion of the PDD Trial hearing in December. Most recent funding has been provided by Gramercy, through two facilities made available on 14 August 2025 (the “August Trance”) and 19 September 2025 (the “September Tranche”). The August Tranche amounted to $65 million; the September Tranche was $30 million. While the August Tranche can be used for Firm overhead but not on specific NOx Group Litigations fees, the September Tranche can, contractually, only be used for the NOx Group Litigations. The funds held are made available by Gramercy &nbsp;and the Firm draws down on cash to service its working capital requirements monthly against these facilities.&nbsp;Anna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, September 30, 2025 5:56 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;In 37.1, we now have duplication in the last two sentences. If we have “The funds held are made available by Gramercy for PG to draw down in line with its cash needs.” Then we don’t need “The Firm draws down on cash to service its working capital requirements monthly against these facilities.” The first sentence is probably better37.4: Matthew Newbould is the leads37.5: Gladson, not Gladston37.7: either “some 12 solicitors working under the Case Leads on the…” or “an additional 12 solicitors on the…”&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 17:44To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: Re: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;All&nbsp;Latest version attached.&nbsp;&nbsp;Re the claimant sols committee - pls could pallas send me a proposed response this evening. I need to be in hospital but back at my desk by 8.30 to finalise and send.&nbsp;Anna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, September 30, 2025 5:28 PMTo: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Xenia Kalognomas &lt;Xenia.Kalognomas@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;On para 22 (and sorry for my confusing draft agreements with executed agreements), do we know that the solicitors are in the process of entering into the agency agreements? If not, I think we should delete para 22 altogether. It isn’t that important&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 16:56To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; A