 to discuss an appropriate way forward with you. Please continue working normally in the meantime.
&nbsp;
Please note that the entirety of your contract of employment remains in place during your notice period. This includes the express obligations set out under clauses 4.2, 16, 17 and 21&nbsp;of the employment contract executed by you with a commencement
 date of 1st September 2022. Your contract also contains implicit contractual obligations as to “good faith and fidelity”.&nbsp; This includes an obligation to act honestly in all dealings with your employer, not working (or conspiring) with a competitor, not disclosing
 our confidential information or trade secrets, not actively disrupting the business or enticing colleagues or clients to leave.&nbsp; To this end, it is notable that a number of your colleagues have chosen to resign contemporaneously.&nbsp; Please be aware that the
 company will not hesitate to take robust action to enforce any breach of your obligations up to and including court action if that becomes necessary. I also bring your attention more generally to the fact that the restrictive covenants at clause 21 of your
 employment contract, which were varied by your agreement on 14th September 2023, continue to remain in effect for up to 6 months after your effective date of termination.
&nbsp;
If you should have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.
&nbsp;
Regards,
