Dear Steer Co and counsel,
&nbsp;
We write regarding the proposal that PG temporarily step back from its role as Lead Solicitor in certain of the group actions.
&nbsp;
For the avoidance of doubt, and as previously explained, &nbsp;PG’s willingness is not to be taken as any admission that PG is unable to continue to fulfil its role. We view the Defendants’ concerns as opportunistic. Our decision is
 made solely in the interests of all Steer Co clients: to reduce distraction from ongoing trial preparation and ensure focus remains on the successful advancement of the claims.
&nbsp;
That said, it is paramount that our clients' interests and interests of the firm continue to be safeguarded. PG is, and will remain, heavily engaged in conducting a very substantial volume of vital trial work which benefits all
 claimants and support the PDD counsel team. In these circumstances, certain protections are non-negotiable and must be agreed in advance in order for PG to consent to this change. For the avoidance of doubt, the below does not reduce or extinguish the rights
 of any steering committee pursuant to the GLOs.
&nbsp;

Delegation of Work


It is imperative to the effective running of the litigation, and a condition to PG agreeing to step back, that the critical Lead Solicitors work that PG is progressing may continue and be properly
 recognised as such.



Accordingly, it should be agreed upfront and in writing that such work be delegated by Leigh Day as remaining Lead Solicitors to PG in relation to each Lead Claim and such work agreed to be
 reasonably incurred.&nbsp;



The Steering Committee authorises such delegation and each Steering Committee accepts liability to pay the reasonable costs for the work done by PG as if it were done by the Steering Committee.&nbsp;



[PG will act as agent of the Steering Committee in relation to such common work and&nbsp;the Steering Committee and the Lead Solicitor authorises PG to perform
 common work in respect of each Steering Committee clients' claims.]&nbsp;&nbsp;



[in accordance with Clause 8 of the Pan Nox Agency Agreement, and under the other Agency Agreements/GLOs as required (to include Cl 8 Ford AA; Cl 8 Nissan AA;
 Cl 8 Peugeot AA; Cl 8 Mercedes AA; [Cl 11 Vauxhall AA]), recognising that where individual GLOs nominate a Steering Committee, the scope and wording of such delegation may differ.]
[I'm still working through the AAs but it's not clear to me how we might rely on clause 8 of the Pan Nox AA. It would be simpler to get the Steer Co and remaining LD to agree the delegation as an overlay to the Pan Nox AA (as discussed yesterday). I have
 not reviewed the other agency agreements yet but grateful if this would be considered in light of that.]


Decision-Making / Settlement Authority
The remaining Lead Solicitors will not make or accept any offer of settlement on behalf of a client which affects the recovery of common costs, sub-group costs and/or Lead and ALGLO costs without
 the agreement, such agreement not to be unreasonably withheld, of the Steering Committee. [check wording in AA]Before the remaining Lead Solicitor makes or accepts any offer of settlement on behalf of a client, they will consult with the Steering Committee.PG/Steering Committee consent will be required before any settlement, discontinuance, or withdrawal that could affect common costs or materially impact PG’s clients (such consent not to be
 unreasonably withheld).PG will retain a veto or joint authority on Lead Claim discontinuance and settlement proposals (noting that settlement is not an issue reserved to the Lead Solicitors by the GLOs).
Costs Protection
Written confirmation for the sake of good order of PG’s entitlement to recover a share of common costs, [sub-group costs and AGLO costs] (per the extant GLOs and AAs) incurred up to the step-down
 date.Protection against liability for common work authorised by others (after the step-down date) without PG’s express approval.



If a defendant is liable to pay any amount in respect of the basic charges or disbursements attributed to PG clients, Leigh Day as the Lead Solicitor may not negotiate directly with that defendant
 without PG's written consent and settle at a level which is less than has been advised to be reasonable by a counsel of 10 or more years call who is recognised by the profession as having expertise in legal costs. Leigh Day will reimburse PG its pro-rated
 share recovered Disbursements within 45 days of receipt&nbsp;from any defendant.


Access to Information
Full access to the Group Register, Discontinued/Terminated Claims Registers, pleadings, expert evidence, CRO matters and settlement communications to be preserved.
Return / Reinstatement Rights
PG will be reinstated as Lead Solicitor with majority agreement of the Steering Committee for [Merc GLO]
&nbsp;and the remaining Lead Solicitors for all other Lead Claims (such agreement not to be unreasonably withheld) upon application to the Court and as soon as possible. [Could we look to tie this to a period of time or event?]&nbsp;
Workstream and Authority Guardrails
Where settlement negotiations include costs-inclusive global offers, PG to have a binding role in Pan-Nox apportionment.
Client Register
No firm on the Steering Committee or acting as Lead Solicitor may directly or indirectly solicit PG’s clients in the Pan Nox litigation.

&nbsp;
The precise implementation of these protections requires careful and urgent discussion, including as to the obvious constitutional differences across the cases. However, confirmation today on the fundamental structure set out
 above is essential. This will enable us to confirm our willingness to step back to the Defendants, and to refocus our energies fully on trial preparation for the benefit of all claimants.
&nbsp;
We trust this approach balances efficiency with the continued protection of client interests, and we look forward to your confirmation, such that we may begin working with you on the necessary agreements and filings.
