rtfall. In regards to those conversations, could you let us know the reason for the increase in the amounts required from the original figures put forward at the start of October?&nbsp;Staged tranches: Gemini operates to adopt the agreed wording on the policy. Given that such payment deadlines on the existing policies have already passed we are enquiring internally how this would operate and be married to your request for staged tranches.&nbsp;As to timings, subject to the finalisation of the flagged queries, we are confident that Gemini quotes will be with you by the end of the week. Just so we are aware, is there a court deadline that we should be aware of in relation to the finalised policies?&nbsp;I am out of the office tomorrow, although Jonathan is around should you have any queries and can pass you any relevant updates as received.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;20 October 2025 18:55To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wt