k.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;28 October 2025 10:21To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Morning James,&nbsp;Please find attached PDD trial week 2 update. &nbsp;&nbsp;Now that the full underwriting overview pack is complete, do you have a sense of when we might receive a preliminary indication from Toremis?&nbsp;Kind regards,Helena&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;27 October 2025 16:56To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Hi James,&nbsp;Please see below update on the other items:&nbsp;PDD Skeleton arguments&nbsp;– please can these be sent through. Please attached.&nbsp;Latest updates and merits opinions – the latest written update we have on these matters is the pan-NOx update from May 2025 (attached). We also have the most recent monthly update on Mercedes. Have any other written updates on merits since been issued from PG or Counsel? If they are available, please can they be provided? We would like to get this pack to Toremis on Monday morning at the latest, so if such notes do not exist there is no need to create them at this stage. No additional substantive advice has been provided, and the submissions have not changed our assessment of the merits.&nbsp;Trial updates and underlying merits advices – we have copies of these documents. We look forward to receiving the PDD trial week 2 update, when available. To follow.&nbsp;Kind regards,Helena&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;27 October 2025 15:45To:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Many thanks Tom. Look forward to receipt of the other items when available.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;27 October 2025 14:04To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Hi James&nbsp;Let us know when works for a call, we will aim to accommodate.&nbsp;Responses are being reviewed for 2 and 3, in the meantime please see below for 1:&nbsp;1. The original LOI approach on 30 September 2025 as was:&nbsp;1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 50% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs (including Non T3 Quantum costs);2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 50% of the Defendants’ claimed cost of cost budgeting;&nbsp;3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 100% of all approved costs to 31 July 2026 (excluding the Tranche 3 PTR, Trial Preparation and Trial phases future approved costs); and4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 0% of all non-approved pending phase costs (Tranche 3 Expert Reports phase and Second General ADR Settlement phase).&nbsp;&nbsp;The updated LOI approach now adopted (based on Cost Counsel advice to be cautious) is:&nbsp;1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 60% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs (including Non T3 Quantum costs);2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 60% of the Defendants’ claimed cost of cost budgeting;&nbsp;3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 100% of all approved costs to 31 July 2026 (including Tranche 3 PTR phase in full, 50% of Trial Preparation&nbsp; phase but still excluding Trial phase future approved costs); and4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 100% of all offered non-approved pending costs for Tranche 3 Expert Reports phase and Second General ADR Settlement phase.&nbsp;We decided to calculate the adverse costs exposure to 31 July 2026 rather than to the conclusion of the budgeted period (December 2026). This is informed by the indication given by Cockerill J on Day 2 of the July PDD PTR that the parties should expect the PDD Judgment to be handed down by July 2026.&nbsp;These percentages of how much work would be incurred by July 2026 are applied not only to the pre-existing Tranche 2 (PDD Trial) and First General cost budgets but also to the Tranche 3 (Quantum Trial) and Second General cost budgets. The calculations exclude the Defendants' costs contained within the Tranche 1 KBA cost budget, as they were unsuccessful in that trial.&nbsp;A further assumption applied is that, in the absence of Court-approved budgeted amounts for certain phases, specifically, Tranche 3 Expert Reports and Second General ADR/Settlement Discussions, the Claimants’ offered figures have been adopted on the basis that these constitute a reasonable estimate of the amounts likely to be approved. Approval of these phases to take place after the January 2026 CMC.&nbsp;Proceeding on the assumption that Judgment in the PDD Trial will be handed down by July 2026 and given that the Tranche 2 PDD and Tranche 3 Quantum cost budgets run concurrently up to that date, it is expected that work relating to the forthcoming Quantum Trial will need to be undertaken irrespective of the outcome.&nbsp;By 31 July 2026, all work undertaken pursuant to Tranche 2 and the First General Costs Budget will have been fully incurred, as the relevant budgeted period runs from June 2024 to April 2026, concluding with the completion of the Spring PDD Trial. In respect of the Tranche 3 and the Second General Costs Budgets it has been necessary to assess the adverse costs exposure by reference to the anticipated progress within each phase as at that date.&nbsp;By 31 July 2026, work would have been fully concluded by the Parties in all of the following phases:&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 CMC·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Selection of the Sample Claimants·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Individual Statements of Case·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Disclosure·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Witness Statements·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 Expert Reports·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tranche 3 PTR&nbsp;At this point, Tranche 3 Co-Ordination Costs will remain outstanding for the working phases. Applying a pro-rata apportionment, 12 months of the 17-month budgeted period will have elapsed, representing approximately 71% of the budget for that phase incurred pre-31 July 2026.&nbsp;The only other phases that will not, at least in part, have concluded by 31 July 2026 are the Tranche 3 Quantum Trial Preparation and Tranche 3 Quantum Trial phases. However, it is foreseeable that the parties will begin to incur costs in respect of counsel’s brief fees for the Quantum Trial from at least Spring 2026 onwards. On that basis, we have adopted the conservative assumption that approximately 50% of this Tranche 3 Quantum Trial Preparation phase will also have been incurred at this point.&nbsp;Similarly, in relation to the Second General Costs Budget, which spans the period April 2026 to December 2026, a comparable pro-rata analysis indicates that, as of 31 July 2026, approximately 44% of the approved costs will have been incurred in the following&nbsp; phases:&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Second General GLO Management Costs (or Pan-NOx Litigation Management Costs)·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Second General ADR/Settlement Discu"}

