To: Ford Litigation Team &lt;fordteam@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;
Subject: Looking Ford-ward 

&nbsp;




Team,


&nbsp;


Over the last few days post the Lead Solicitor application, I and the other case leads, have been engaging with LD to establish what our
brave new world&nbsp;will look like and how the teams implement it.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


Ultimately, whether we like it or not (and barring the Court going completely left field in their judgment tomorrow), LD are going to be the sole Lead Solicitor
 on the Ford Litigation. I am genuinely sorry that this has happened and that things have happened the way that they have. None of you deserve to the subject to this. This juncture has been reached through no fault of any of yours and believe me when I say
 I know just how unpleasant it feels. I also fully appreciate that it sucks even more to know that, despite how much it feels like we've been relegated to &quot;just another claimant firm&quot;, we will still need to perform largely the same role that we have been before
 now - except we do it without the title of Lead Solicitor.&nbsp;&nbsp;


&nbsp;


As we try to gather some understanding of how this new world will practically work, especially with the Agency Agreement that the firms have executed, there
 are a few things that look to have been decided that I can inform you of:


&nbsp;



The AA (as the firms have executed) puts me under the supervision of LD - it does not extend to you as individuals. You
 will still work under PG and your day jobs go on as normal. How this works for me and my instructions to you, we are all trying to get to the bottom of. You are all smart lawyers and I am sure you can appreciate that I may have some concerns over how this
 works in practice, but I (and the other case leads) will be doing what we can to a) ensure you are fully equipped and supported to do you job and b) find a solution that works for everyone so we can move forward;



LD will take over all comms (incoming and outgoing) to the Ds. As part of the AA that the firms have agreed, I will
 be CC'ed on those emails, and I will then need to pass them onto the team along with instructions;



Similar with external meetings with the Defendants. The de facto is that LD will attend these solo but there will
 inevitably be instances where PG team members are needed;



Communications with counsel etc can (I believe) proceed as normal and we shouldn't have to run these past LD, but if that
 changes, I will let you know;



All external work on the PG SharePoint that is &quot;common work&quot; will at some stage be moved over to the LD SharePoint - this
 is to ensure links going out to the Ds etc go from a Leigh Day email account (the timeline on this is very much TBC becuase of how big of a task it is);



Group Register (and Notice of Objection) work has not yet been decided but §19 of the Ford GLO dictates that PG have responsibility
 for this, not the Lead Solicitor, so it is likely that this will remain as it has been. I will update on this when I know more;



Trial preparation and attendance is expected to be as it would have been otherwise. I have been today working on a rota
 for who will be where, when. There is also a suggestion that we may work from LD for the week(s) before the trial to make preparation and communication easier. This sounds like a very good idea to me and I will update on this when I know more.


&nbsp;


It's not all doom and gloom. The entire LD team, especially the LD Ford team and Nichola in particular, know how difficult a time this is for us collectively
 and all of you as individuals. They are immensely appreciative of all of the work that we are doing and they understand that collaboration between us must continue elsewise there is every chance things will fall over.&nbsp;


&nbsp;


We will keep plugging on and I will keep you all as informed as I can over the coming days and weeks. One piece of good news (if you choose to take it as
 good news) is that I will be in the office almost weekly from now until I depart for my new role, starting from next week. We have opening submissions on Monday and Tuesday - let's arrange to do a team lunch, or heaven forbid a drink post-work, one of the
 days next week to celebrate having got this insanely massive piece of litigation to trial within 2 years of making the GLO application - that in itself is insane never mind what we have been through over the last 2 years (and 2 months). I say this often, but
 I am genuinely astonished at how freakishly competent you all are at your jobs and I am very very proud to work alongside all of you. You are all an absolute credit.


&nbsp;


As always, I'm around if anyone wants to chat or discuss anything in the email.


&nbsp;


Thanks,


&nbsp;


Michael

































​​​​


































