r to the mechanism in clause 1(b) of the BHP 4th&nbsp;excess reimbursement deed. It will be difficult to justify a circumstance where it has been given in relation to the BHP 4th&nbsp;excess reimbursement deed but not for Toremis’ proposal, where the intention behind both structures is the same.&nbsp;Could you please confirm that this works? In the meantime, we asked if they could agree in principle to cap the amount to be provisioned/ring fenced by PG, as we have both in the wrapper deed and in clause 1(b) of the 4th&nbsp;layer reimbursement deed.&nbsp;We appreciate your prompt attention to this matter, given the time constraints.&nbsp;Kind regards&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;11 November 2025 15:22To:&nbsp;Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;; Josh O'Melia &lt;jomelia@gramercy.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - Toremis&nbsp;Thanks Nick&nbsp;Just sent the invite&nbsp;Tom&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708From:&nbsp;Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;11 November 2025 18:20To:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;; Josh O'Melia &lt;jomelia@gramercy.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; H