empt to stabilise matters asap.&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Thursday, November 6, 2025 3:13:37 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Counsel CFAs &nbsp;Hi Anna,&nbsp;The Credit Agreement and the portfolio insurance backing Gramercy’s debt set out a level of fees with third parties that PG can incur before requiring Gramercy’s approval.&nbsp;If those limits are exceeded, approval must be obtained. The rationale is that success fees are added on top of Gramercy’s repayment, so the structure is based on specific financial assumptions. Otherwise, they need to be subordinated to Gramercy.&nbsp;If we can confirm that the additional barristers’ projected success fees remain within the agreed limits under Schedule III of the Credit Agreement, then approval would not be required. We were seeking approval out of caution, as I am not certain of our current position in relation to the fee limits. But Tom C may be able to help.&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 11:44To: Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Counsel CFAs&nbsp;(Removing the leavers from email chain)&nbsp;Dilan - thanks. Please may I understand why G are signing off on these CFA's? This is why ppl have concerns about the control they exert. Is there any way of speeding this along pls or better yet just moving forward. I dont fancy being chased again. Sarah tells me we have been sat on these for quite some time