nated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Tom,&nbsp;Thanks for your emails on this and apologies for not getting back to you on this until now – I have been in and out of meetings all day.&nbsp;One of these meetings was to discuss the applicability of Gemini to the below requests and to review the numbers you sent through. Internally and with the insurance carriers sitting behind Gemini we are just bottoming out a few queries as to the applicability of Gemini to these matters, but so far we are confident that cover can be sourced from Gemini subject to the below points:Gemini operates as a follow-on facility to co-insured policies. Gemini capacity can therefore be added to all your matters except for the following, where there is only one insurer on the relevant policy layers:Hyundai-Kia – Primary &amp; ExcessRenault – 2nd&nbsp;excessToyota – PrimaryGemini can offer a maximum of 12.5% additional capacity in relation to in-scope policies.&nbsp;Looking at the numbers you have sent through, and the effect of point 1 above, Gemini can therefore fully cover the required amounts for FCA and Mazda and a significant portion of your other requests. I am just confirming the exact amounts internally and will let you know when we have them.&nbsp;We will continue to see what we can do in relation to the open market as to the shortfall. In regards to those conversations, could you let us know the reason for the increase in the amounts required from the original figures put forward at the start of October?&nbsp;Staged tranches: Gemini operates to adopt the agreed wording on the policy. Given that such payment deadlines on the existing policies have already passed we are enquiring internally how this would operate and be married to your request for staged tranches.&nbsp;As to timings, subject to the finalisation of the flagged queries, we are confident that Gemini quotes will be with you by the end of the week. Just so we are aware, is there a court deadline that we should be aware of in relation to the finalised policies?&nbsp;I am out of the office tomorrow, although Jonathan is around should you have any queries and can pass you any relevant updates as received.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;20 October 2025 18:55To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;jonathan.simon@wtwco.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Hi James&nbsp;See below analysis of the LOI topupo required across the emissions cases. The table also shows when the incremental LOI requirement would apply, based on estimated adverse costs 