Raminder,&nbsp;As you know Leila is arguing that our analysis of her contractual position isn’t correct.&nbsp; She’s sent me the attached emails.&nbsp; If she isn’t a contractor but is actually an employee does that affect her tax position? &nbsp;&nbsp;Howard&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for Mac &nbsp;​​​​Howard&nbsp;MorrisChairmanFrom: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Monday, 22 September 2025 at 18:18To: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsHi Howard &nbsp;Thanks again for your time today. I attach a few emails on a WP basis as discussed in relation to my entitlements (and my Partner promotion for reference). Look forward to speaking on Wednesday or, Thursday.&nbsp;Thank you.&nbsp;​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696From: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Monday, 22 September 2025 at 07:35To: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsHi Howard,&nbsp;That’s great.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you.&nbsp;Best,​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696From: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, September 22, 2025 6:43:02 AMTo: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To Costs &nbsp;Leila,&nbsp;May we speak at 5.15PM BST?&nbsp;Howard&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for Mac &nbsp;​​​​Howard&nbsp;MorrisChairmanFrom: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, 19 September 2025 at 19:52To: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsHi Howard&nbsp;Are you available for a WP meeting about this?&nbsp;Thank you&nbsp;&nbsp;Best,​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696From: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Friday, September 19, 2025 3:37:52 PMTo: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To Costs &nbsp;Without Prejudice and Subject to Contract&nbsp;Dear Leila, &nbsp;&nbsp;I am sorry that I’ve been slower in replying than I wanted.&nbsp; Further to our recent discussions and your email of 16 September, your comments are noted and it is clear you have shown great commitment to the firm since joining us as a Contractor.&nbsp;&nbsp;I, the firm, appreciates the reasons behind the exit arrangements you have proposed; however, we are not in a position to agree to those terms.&nbsp;Please see below our own offer for your consideration. If we are unable to reach a final agreement, you may choose to continue with the Firm as a Contractor or give notice to terminate your agreement.We would like you to work your three-month notice period to ensure a smooth handover and transition. This would mean your contract would come to an end on 31 December 2025.In recognition of your hard work and commitment, we are prepared to offer you a payment equivalent to two months of your standard consultancy fees (£20,833).&nbsp;We appreciate that these terms may not meet your full expectations. However, as you are engaged with the firm on a Contractor basis rather than as an employee, we are limited to the terms of your consultancy agreement and are unable to provide additional benefits or enhanced termination terms beyond what is contractually agreed. Our offer above is therefore intended as a gesture of goodwill in recognition of the contribution you have made during your time with us.&nbsp;I look forward to receiving your response.&nbsp;Best wishes,&nbsp;Howard&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for Mac &nbsp;​​​​Howard&nbsp;MorrisChairmanFrom: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, 19 September 2025 at 13:16To: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsDear Howard,&nbsp;As you indicated I would receive a response by today I wanted to follow up on this before it gets too late, in your Friday afternoon.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you&nbsp;Best,​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696From:&nbsp;Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, September 17, 2025 12:03 PMTo:&nbsp;Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Without Prejudice Save as To Costs&nbsp;Thank you, Howard.&nbsp;​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696From: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Wednesday, 17 September 2025 at 12:02To: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsLeila, by Friday.&nbsp;Best wishes,&nbsp;Howard&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for Mac&nbsp;​​​​Howard&nbsp;MorrisChairmanFrom: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Wednesday, 17 September 2025 at 15:54To: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsThank you, Howard.&nbsp;I would be grateful if you could confirm the expected date by which you will be able to return to me on the below.&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696From: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Tuesday, 16 September 2025 at 04:09To: Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Without Prejudice Save as To CostsLeila,&nbsp;Thanks. I will get back to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;Howard&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Howard&nbsp;MorrisChairmanFrom:&nbsp;Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Tuesday, September 16, 2025 12:29:29 AMTo:&nbsp;Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Without Prejudice Save as To Costs&nbsp;WPSTCDear Howard,I refer to our WP meeting today, Monday 15 September 2025 and my various emails since the Board’s inception as referred to below. I am very grateful for your time with this matter, and I welcome the opportunity to have a constructive conversation.As you know, I have raised a number of concerns in recent weeks, most recently in my email of Wednesday 10 September 2025, and previously both individually and with other Partners since the Board appointment. These concerns arise in relation to the firm’s governance, funding uncertainty, exclusion from LATAM decision-making and deteriorating client and external collaborator relationships. Taken together and as previously flagged, these issues create significant regulatory and professional exposure for both the firm and me (particularly in relation to Brazil and Peru matters) and have caused ongoing detriment to me both professionally and personally.As we discussed, these issues have materially impacted my ability to execute my duties, leaving me effectively sidelined and to date little has been done to alleviate the risks.(1) Repsol Peruvian CaseIn particular, the representations made to tens of thousands of Peruvian clients and to the Dutch Stichting, the precarious funding position (that I was recently made aware of) and both the firm’s and my own professional obligations to such clients who have assigned their claims to the Dutch Stitchting, at the firm’s direction.(2) Brazil OperationsIn respect of Brazil matters, I have sought clarity on budgeting and operations (an area of my significant prior involvement) and in particular the imminent operational restructuring. Despite several requests and assurances that information would be provided, no information or engagement has been provided to date but for, an FHA cashflow (sent on 11 September) which was without any parameters or, objectives as to the degree of cuts to be made.As previously mentioned, and in respect of both matters above, I have relocated for the firm twice over the past 3.5 years, taking on considerable personal and professional risk to establish and expand the&nbsp;LATAM practice. This relocation involved moving my family internationally and the taking out of a new lease in Brazil while also continuing to meet ongoing housing-related financial obligations in our previous country of residence. This lease, for context, was entered into at the firm’s request and is in my personal name. Should I need to leave Brazil immediately my prior home accommodation would not be available.Exit TermsI understand that you wish to reflect on how these matters might be resolved, but you also ask that I set out my terms for an exit should no viable solution prove possible. For the sake of time, I briefly set out those exit terms below.Subject to contract, on the following basis:Three months payment in lieu of my notice period.A net of tax, ex-gratia payment representing 12 months’ salary.International relocation costs, including flights (business class flights) and the shipment of belongings for my family and I, or the cash equivalent.Payment of the lease (and associated costs) at my residence in Brazil until it expires in June 2026.Payment of all legal fees incurred, without waiver of privilege.I would require any agreement to cover the above points. In return, I would be prepared to agree to confidential terms in said agreement, to resolve matters amicably including to waive any future claims against the firm, to waive any right to pursue various financial promises made to me throughout my tenure (including synthetic equity bonuses and discretionary bonuses, to name a few). I hope we can agree this fairly, in a way that reflects my contribution to the firm and allows me to leave on the right terms should that be the best course of action.I look forward to your response.Best regards,&nbsp;​​​​Leila‑Zoe&nbsp;MezoughiPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;696&nbsp;"}

