Thanks both – agreed, the tone of the call was constructive. &nbsp;Please see attached the 24 Sept letter referred to in the Renault notice Alessia asked for. &nbsp;On the heads of terms, it sounds like Lizzy Comley (Slaters) may already be putting something together, which we will share as soon as it comes through. Subject to that, I think it’d be great if you could hold the pen on getting those together. &nbsp;Additionally, noting that the Renault application asked for confirmation by 4pm of whether we could provide the request information, we have prepared the short draft email below. If we’re not able to get the broader letter to the Defendants out in the next letter, we’d propose sending this. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:45To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Draft email to Ds on stepping down&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Jessica. It sounds very positive.&nbsp;Would you like us to write up the detailed heads of terms?&nbsp;When we get back your comments on the witness statement, we will update it to take account of these developments (just the progress to agreement, not the details).&nbsp;We will also look at the Freshfields letter and consider if we need to refer to it now (probably not), or deal with it later.&nbsp;Matt&nbsp;&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nb