Hi all

&nbsp;

I have reviewed the attached and made some comments on the document.

&nbsp;

I don’t think this document is any improvement on their last memo in terms of the issues in the approach, sadly.

&nbsp;

There is further work we could do to try to address some of the issues in here which I have noted in my comments, but none of these would address the fundamental issues with the approach. Hopefully when we get their second note
 on Monday that will be more relevant and we can consider this in the round.

&nbsp;

We can then decide after the con with counsel on Tuesday whether this is worth engaging with any further and whether we will send any comments on this memo back to them.

&nbsp;

I do think it would be worth a short message to them now to confirm the following before our con – draft below which I plan to send tomorrow.

&nbsp;

Dear Steve, Nielson and team

&nbsp;

We have had a further chance to review your updated memo. Thank you for the work that has gone into this.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

We do still have some concerns about the approach, but will wait for your further note before sending any substantive comments over.

&nbsp;

We will be discussing both notes with the counsel team on Tuesday.&nbsp; We would be grateful if you could hold off on further work on this with the updated claimant data until after that. We will come back as soon as we can with
 an update.

&nbsp;

We note from your email below that you may be able to add calculations based on the “illegality” and “cost of cure” approaches, pending further discussions and the availability of required inputs. Please can you include in your
 note that is coming on Monday as much information as possible about what inputs you would need and the timescales for putting figures to those.

&nbsp;

We note it is not possible to conduct an event study in advance of the December 17 deadline.&nbsp;Do you have any observations on the data received that you could share at this stage?&nbsp; Can you see any helpful trends / issues we need
 to be aware of?&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Best wishes

&nbsp;


